bent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor JB Pritzker seeks a third term against Darren Bailey, the downstate Republican he defeated by roughly twelve points in 2022. Illinois' six-point Democratic lean, a midterm environment favoring the incumbent's party, and Pritzker's vast self-funded war chest frame the contest. He is outspending Bailey's campaign about twenty-five to one, and the two met in a single, contentious mid-October debate covering taxes, Trump, and the Bears stadium.\n\nEvery major race rating places Illinois in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and recent polls show Pritzker ahead about twenty points, 54 to 34 percent. Prediction markets price his win probability in the mid-nineties. Bailey's path runs through heavy downstate turnout and a nationalized backlash against the incumbent, but with limited resources and no visible polling movement, the evidence points to a comfortable Pritzker re-election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "20